      "type": "text",
      "text": "{\"id\":\"THE-608\",\"uuid\":\"d7cc2faa-b1c2-4c06-a548-6c8355fe832b\",\"title\":\"Keep merge-drain error diagnostics separate from conflict-path metadata\",\"description\":\"## Finding\\n\\nThe in-process merge driver passes its diagnostic `detail` as the fourth argument of `update_merge_status(worktree, status, result_oid, conflict_paths, error_detail)`, and passes None as the fifth. At crates/thegn-host/src/merge_driver.rs, the `set` closure calls `update_merge_status(..., oid, detail, None)`. The trait and SQLite implementation in store/worktree_aux.rs and db_aux.rs clearly define the opposite semantic slot for a general error diagnostic.\\n\\nConsequently a canonical-history gate error is persisted as purported conflict paths and leaves error_detail empty. This corrupts queue presentation and downstream branch-failure interpretation. It is independent of whether the underlying gate correctly refuses the operation.\\n\\n## Actual evidence\\n\\nFull configured source4 queue gate (18 frozen paths; nextest a40d4351-55ec-4b79-8b3b-7ddeac5c8ad9, session99446 exit100) passed its three contract stages and 4746 workspace tests before the daemon authenticated route-to-host regression stopped at held.conflict_paths.is_none(). It had already observed gate_error and unchanged attempts/no result OID. Source trace above proves the wrong argument order; this is not a fixture representation error. Log /tmp/thegn-audit/tasks/merge-queue-combined-full-tests2.log, SHA256 70fb8772e031b013fe1e0a172356df306400b3d1fac2d96486aea74bb6393f7b.\\n\\n## Required repair\\n\\nCorrect the argument semantics at the driver boundary. Keep error reasons/logs in error_detail; actual newline-separated merge-conflict paths alone belong in conflict_paths. Audit all status transitions through the shared closure, including retry/folding and terminal states. Do not silently retain stale conflict or error metadata when a new attempted result supersedes it; preserve the store's documented None-means-unchanged behavior rather than changing that generic API without review.\\n\\nAdd focused real private SQLite regressions for gate_error diagnostic persistence (no conflict paths or success OID, no agent blame), real deferred conflicts (actual paths not prose), and relevant retry transitions. Preserve the authenticated transport tests and their strict assertions. Do not ignore tests or weaken canonical-history admission.\\n\\n## Dependencies and delivery\\n\\nCompanion correction in the reviewed local queue-safety integration; blocks <issue id=\\\"ad1f26f7-c577-40d2-81ef-2b44c608c63c\\\" href=\\\"https://linear.app/blakeashley/issue/THE-586/reconcile-delivery-inventory-for-the-landed-validation-severity-change\\\">THE-586</issue> live retry until exact focused/full/fixed-binary native gates pass. Related <issue id=\\\"350043aa-7616-46fe-b4f0-041ee58d9b23\\\" href=\\\"https://linear.app/blakeashley/issue/THE-589/do-not-persist-or-report-speculative-folds-as-landed-when-gate-or\\\">THE-589</issue> outcome truth, <issue id=\\\"ec8dec1e-dc34-4972-8b28-b3ae75cb85e3\\\" href=\\\"https://linear.app/blakeashley/issue/THE-591/persist-final-merge-outcomes-atomically-without-transiently-requeueing\\\">THE-591</issue> atomic bookkeeping, <issue id=\\\"c6c9f3aa-5720-492e-b5cb-47d749dcbab5\\\" href=\\\"https://linear.app/blakeashley/issue/THE-606/require-canonical-git-history-before-fold-results-and-destructive\\\">THE-606</issue> canonical history. Normal source review and commit hooks required. No live DB rewrite, merge, cleanup or push is authorized by this issue; the ongoing user-approved local merge workflow retains its existing gates.\",\"priority\":{\"value\":2,\"name\":\"High\"},\"url\":\"https://linear.app/blakeashley/issue/THE-608/keep-merge-drain-error-diagnostics-separate-from-conflict-path\",\"gitBranchName\":\"blake/the-608-keep-merge-drain-error-diagnostics-separate-from-conflict\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-09-12T07:04:39.729Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-09-14T23:01:43.228Z\",\"archivedAt\":null,\"completedAt\":null,\"startedAt\":\"2026-09-12T07:04:39.839Z\",\"canceledAt\":null,\"dueDate\":null,\"slaStartedAt\":null,\"slaMediumRiskAt\":null,\"slaHighRiskAt\":null,\"slaBreachesAt\":null,\"status\":\"In Progress\",\"statusType\":\"started\",\"labels\":[],\"attachments\":[],\"documents\":[],\"stateHistory\":[{\"state\":{\"id\":\"1dad59ac-6f23-4363-95ca-f256f00ff767\",\"name\":\"In Progress\",\"type\":\"started\"},\"startedAt\":\"2026-09-12T07:04:39.729Z\",\"endedAt\":null}],\"createdBy\":\"Blake Ashley\",\"createdById\":\"3b7f5427-3d7f-40df-822c-6b4439a509e7\",\"project\":\"Runtime Security & Host Architecture\",\"projectId\":\"b3843a6d-8684-4f3e-b4da-13b36a6728ef\",\"parentId\":\"THE-588\",\"team\":\"Thegn\",\"teamId\":\"6d265c7c-ac1f-40c7-9983-f919d7b5d254\",\"relations\":{\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"THE-586\",\"title\":\"Reconcile delivery inventory for the landed validation-severity change\"}],\"blockedBy\":[],\"relatedTo\":[{\"id\":\"THE-606\",\"title\":\"Require canonical Git history before fold results and destructive merge cleanup\"},{\"id\":\"THE-589\",\"title\":\"Do not persist or report speculative folds as landed when gate or target advancement fails\"},{\"id\":\"THE-591\",\"title\":\"Persist final merge outcomes atomically without transiently requeueing held candidates\"},{\"id\":\"THE-638\",\"title\":\"Maintenance batch 03: task-manager performance and ten scoped bug acceptances\"},{\"id\":\"THE-219\",\"title\":\"Stop merge drain after an agent isolation-floor infrastructure hold\"},{\"id\":\"THE-610\",\"title\":\"Stop merge-drain retry when agent isolation admission is held\"}],\"duplicateOf\":null}}"
    }
  ]
